{"author":{"affiliation_history":[{"country_code":"US","id":"I129510320","name":"University of Wisconsin\u2013Green Bay","years":[2024,2025,2026]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I4405266016","name":"Hopkins Marine Station","years":[2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I97018004","name":"Stanford University","years":[2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I1304256225","name":"University of Wisconsin System","years":[2024,2025]},{"country_code":"CA","id":"I141945490","name":"University of British Columbia","years":[2012,2015,2016,2017,2018,2021]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I103635307","name":"University of California, Riverside","years":[2012]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I6750721","name":"University of Montana","years":[2006,2008,2009]}],"author_id":"A5046979471","ca_plastic_works_count":0,"ca_works_count":1,"citations_by_year":[{"all":44,"plastic":0,"year":2017},{"all":70,"plastic":0,"year":2018},{"all":107,"plastic":0,"year":2019},{"all":175,"plastic":0,"year":2020},{"all":193,"plastic":0,"year":2021},{"all":243,"plastic":0,"year":2022},{"all":213,"plastic":0,"year":2023},{"all":223,"plastic":2,"year":2024},{"all":252,"plastic":4,"year":2025},{"all":233,"plastic":1,"year":2026}],"cited_by_count":1940,"current_in_ca":false,"domain_tags":[],"early_career":false,"first_pub_year":2006,"first_year":2024,"h_index":24,"institution_ids":["I129510320","I4405266016","I97018004"],"last_ca_year":2025,"last_year":2024,"m_quotient":1.2,"name":"Paolo S. Segre","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2396-2670","plastic_basis":"openalex","plastic_citations":7,"plastic_works_count":1,"primary_affiliations":[{"country_code":"US","id":"I129510320","name":"University of Wisconsin\u2013Green Bay","source":"openalex_last_known"}],"rising_pct":null,"rising_score":null,"work_count":1,"work_ids":["W4391889663"]},"profile":{"bio":"","keywords":[],"links":[{"label":"Segre ecophysiology lab website","url":"https://segre-ecophysiology-lab.github.io/"}]},"schema_version":"s3.1","works":[{"abstract":"The sensory mechanisms used by baleen whales (Mysticeti) for locating ephemeral, dense prey patches in vast marine habitats are poorly understood. Baleen whales have a functional olfactory system with paired rather than single blowholes (nares), potentially enabling stereo-olfaction. Dimethyl sulfide (DMS) is an odorous gas emitted by phytoplankton in response to grazing by zooplankton. Some seabirds use DMS to locate prey, but this ability has not been demonstrated in whales. For 14 extant species of baleen whale, nares morphometrics (imagery from unoccupied aerial systems, UAS) was related to published trophic level indices using Bayesian phylogenetic mixed modelling. A significant negative relationship was found between nares width and whale trophic level ( \u03b2 = \u22120.08, lower 95% CI = \u22120.13, upper 95% CI = \u22120.03), corresponding with a 39% increase in nares width from highest to lowest trophic level. Thus, species with nasal morphology best suited to stereo-olfaction are more zooplanktivorous. These findings provide evidence that some baleen whale species may be able to localize odorants e.g. DMS. Our results help direct future behavioural trials of olfaction in baleen whales, by highlighting the most appropriate species to study. This is a research priority, given the potential for DMS-mediated plastic ingestion by whales.","author_count":18,"author_ids":["A5009201508","A5026157227","A5033587830","A5037425056","A5039814359","A5044811976","A5046631188","A5046979471","A5048063628","A5048259583","A5051144377","A5059800806","A5060412365","A5075521041","A5077229402","A5078816863","A5079865212","A5122307436"],"author_institution_ids":["I129510320","I4405266016","I97018004"],"authors":[{"id":"A5009201508","name":"Conor Ryan"},{"id":"A5122307436","name":"Maria Clara Iruzun Martins"},{"id":"A5078816863","name":"Kevin Healy"},{"id":"A5048259583","name":"Lars Bejder"},{"id":"A5059800806","name":"Salvatore Cerchio"},{"id":"A5077229402","name":"Fredrik Christiansen"},{"id":"A5051144377","name":"John W. Durban"},{"id":"A5026157227","name":"Holly Fearnbach"},{"id":"A5048063628","name":"Sarah M. E. Fortune"},{"id":"A5039814359","name":"Ari S. Friedlaender"},{"id":"A5075521041","name":"William R. Koski"},{"id":"A5044811976","name":"Carolyn A. Miller"},{"id":"A5079865212","name":"Fabian Rodr\u00edguez-Gonz\u00e1lez"},{"id":"A5046979471","name":"Paolo S. Segre"},{"id":"A5060412365","name":"Jorge Urb\u00e1n R."},{"id":"A5037425056","name":"Fabien Vivier"},{"id":"A5046631188","name":"Caroline R. Weir"},{"id":"A5033587830","name":"Michael John Moore"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":7,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1098/rsbl.2023.0479","domain_tags":["ecotoxicology_and_trophic_transfer","human_exposure_and_health_risk"],"facet_tags":["matrix:marine"],"institution_ids":["I117965899","I129510320","I129902397","I16835326","I185103710","I188760350","I204337017","I4210097969","I4405266016","I4405273082","I66958751","I84038732","I88170914","I97018004"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Biology Letters","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"bronze","oa_url":"https://royalsocietypublishing.org/doi/pdf/10.1098/rsbl.2023.0479","openalex_topics":["T10659","T10971","T13100"],"plastic_related":false,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10659","pub_date":"2024-01-01","study_type":"article","title":"Morphology of nares associated with stereo-olfaction in baleen whales","type":"article","work_id":"W4391889663","year":2024}]}
